-- found by the cubicaltt leg (M20 F4), 2026-09-27: unglue does not look through a definition application
-- eezott REJECTS this: 'the path's left endpoint is suc one, expected unglue (g i1)'. unglue (g i1) must be two:
-- g i1 = glue [] two and unglue (glue ts a) = a. The scrutinee of unglue arrives as a rigid definition application
-- (the H_DEF plan) and vunglue does not unfold it; the normal form of unglue (g i1) is itself, and it converts with nothing.
def G (i : I) : U := Glue Nat (~ i) [ ~ i -> (Nat , idEquiv Nat) ]
def g (i : I) : G i := glue [ ~ i -> two ] two
def main : Path Nat (unglue (g i1)) two := \_ -> two
